<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Wed.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves into the banking system via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements (RPs) Wednesday, the New York Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The action was expected. Fed funds were trading at 5 3/8 percent, slightly above the current official target level of 5 1/4 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663 ))</p>
